[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2831362027","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105767#issuecomment-2831362027","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105767","id":2831362027,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6owyfr","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-25T20:22:09Z","updated_at":"2025-04-25T20:22:09Z","body":"Seems like it was introduced in 3.0, but was already unused back then (as of `3.0-stable` at least):\r\n```\r\ncore/os/memory.cpp\r\n73:uint64_t Memory::alloc_count = 0;\r\n87:     atomic_increment(&alloc_count);\r\n169:    atomic_decrement(&alloc_count);\r\n\r\ncore/os/memory.h\r\n53:     static uint64_t alloc_count;\r\n```","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2831362027/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2831381308","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105767#issuecomment-2831381308","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105767","id":2831381308,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ow3M8","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-25T20:34:22Z","updated_at":"2025-04-25T20:35:05Z","body":"I believe this variable would allow creating a new performance monitor so you can monitor the number of allocations performed each second. I recall @lawnjelly mentioned this at some point. See https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/62291#issuecomment-1162196287 near the top.\r\n\r\nIt does mention this though:\r\n\r\n>  (time spent computation only compiled in debug builds as the clock sampling itself it is a performance hit).\r\n\r\nSo if we decide to keep it, it should be enabled in debug builds only.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2831381308/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2831385301","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105767#issuecomment-2831385301","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105767","id":2831385301,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ow4LV","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-25T20:36:49Z","updated_at":"2025-04-25T20:36:49Z","body":"> I believe this variable would allow creating a new performance monitor so you can monitor the number of allocations performed each second. I recall @lawnjelly mentioned this at some point. See [#62291 (comment)](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/62291#issuecomment-1162196287) near the top.\r\n> \r\n> It does mention this though:\r\n> \r\n> > (time spent computation only compiled in debug builds as the clock sampling itself it is a performance hit).\r\n> \r\n> So if we decide to keep it, it should be enabled in debug builds only.\r\n\r\nAllocation monitoring can be done with profilers. I don't think we need to do an in-house version, especially for only parts of allocations :)","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2831385301/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2831386533","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105767#issuecomment-2831386533","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105767","id":2831386533,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ow4el","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-25T20:37:32Z","updated_at":"2025-04-25T20:38:43Z","body":"We've noticed this and discussed it before. In the past we agreed to expose it to the counters as Calinou mentioned. \r\n\r\nDario made a nice PR already actually, but we never decided on it https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/92206\r\n\r\nThe benefit of using monitors is that it is exposed to our users. Its fine for us to use external tools, but if memory allocations are an issue for games (and they are: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/62291#issuecomment-1162196287) then users need to be able to diagnose the issue and make changes to their game to address it\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2831386533/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2831402067","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105767#issuecomment-2831402067","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105767","id":2831402067,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ow8RT","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-25T20:46:59Z","updated_at":"2025-04-25T20:49:09Z","body":"> We've noticed this and discussed it before. In the past we agreed to expose it to the counters as Calinou mentioned.\r\n> \r\n> Dario made a nice PR already actually, but we never decided on it #92206\r\n> \r\n> The benefit of using monitors is that it is exposed to our users. Its fine for us to use external tools, but if memory allocations are an issue for games (and they are: [#62291 (comment)](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/62291#issuecomment-1162196287)) then users need to be able to diagnose the issue and make changes to their game to address it\r\n\r\nWhile giving users tools to track allocation is a good endeavour, I'm not sure how useful tracking static memory specifically is. It's only part of all actual allocations (most of which go through `memnew` instead, I think).\r\n\r\n> users need to be able to diagnose the issue and make changes to their game to address it\r\n\r\nApple Instruments is pretty accessible (I'm not sure about other operating systems). And we do have a bit of coverage on the docs: https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/contributing/development/debugging/using_cpp_profilers.html\r\nAs you know, these contain statistics, call stacks, and allocation type.\r\nIn comparison, one number keeping track of the count (or even the number of bytes) doesn't seem all that useful to me.\r\n\r\nAll in all, at a cost of 15% to allocation performance, this tracking feels just far too niché to me.\r\nIf we _really_ need to keep it, we should at least pack it into a setting of some kind (e.g. Memory.track_allocation_counts = true`). That should mitigate the idle tracking cost.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2831402067/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2831409378","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105767#issuecomment-2831409378","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105767","id":2831409378,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ow-Di","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-25T20:51:35Z","updated_at":"2025-04-25T20:59:17Z","body":"IMO since we aren't using it currently and it has a significant measured performance cost, there's no reason not to remove it.\r\n\r\nWhile rebasing #92206 (which is now stale almost for a year), it can be re-added, and we can evaluate whether the performance tradeoffs are worth the added debugging information (could be at least kept for `DEBUG_ENABLED` only for example). In other words, we should treat this as a new feature and not rely on the fact that we have some dead code to potentially make use of.\r\n\r\nI do agree that having more information present in Godot's own profilers is important. External profilers are great and more powerful but also only tools power users would use. Godot's goal is to make this kind of thing accessible to everyone, at the cost of less feature completeness and flexibility.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2831409378/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2831436618","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105767#issuecomment-2831436618","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105767","id":2831436618,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6oxEtK","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-25T21:09:56Z","updated_at":"2025-04-25T21:09:56Z","body":"> While giving users tools to track allocation is a good endeavour, I'm not sure how useful tracking static memory specifically is. It's only part of all actual allocations (most of which go through memnew instead, I think).\r\n\r\nThat's a good point, and part of why Dario's previous PR wasn't merged. We need to step back and think about exactly what we track and how we expose it to users. (i.e. allocations per second vs. overall allocations vs. allocations per frame).\r\n\r\nI'm happy to concede to you and Akien. Let's remove it for now and then implement a proper monitor for tracking memory allocations later","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2831436618/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2831604127","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105767#issuecomment-2831604127","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105767","id":2831604127,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6oxtmf","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-25T23:30:34Z","updated_at":"2025-04-25T23:30:34Z","body":"Thanks!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2831604127/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]